;; Negative fixture: unprimed generic head with space inside <...> — must lex-error (unclosed
;; bracket). Arc 109 "the comma dies in the reader" retired the comma-carrying multi-param
;; spelling this fixture originally used (`<nil, nil>`) — see the sibling `_primed_space`
;; fixture's comment for why a single-param bracket (`<nil >`) is the honest replacement.
(:wat::core::defn :user::take [m <- :wat::core::HashMap<wat::core::nil >] -> :wat::core::nil nil)
